    <briefdescription>
<para>Issues and validates the HS256 JWTs that authenticate clients. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Token parameters (issuer, type, validity and secret) come from the <ref refid="classConfigurator" kindref="compound">Configurator</ref> via <ref refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1KeeprBase" kindref="compound">KeeprBase</ref>. Generated tokens carry identity claims and last-logout time so a later logout can be detected. Validation first decodes the token into the <ref refid="structClientLoginData" kindref="compound">ClientLoginData</ref>, then verifies it with <ref refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1KeeprBase_1a42038514e4e95779bf05a6f5d1ecad44" kindref="member">KeeprBase::validateToken</ref>; the coroutine form awaits the async variant. <simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classapi_1_1v2_1_1KeeprBase" kindref="compound">KeeprBase</ref> In everyday words: this class is like a badge printer and badge checker. It stamps a badge with the user&apos;s identity and an expiry, and later checks that a presented badge is genuine and still current. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
